---
// How the parts relate: scans, then the Heart Twin, then two branches. Still boxes and arrows, so it reads the same on a
// phone and with reduced motion.
---
<div class="tmap" role="img" aria-label="How the parts relate. Chest scans go into the Heart Twin, a simulated heart in a scanned chest. From the twin come two branches. Branch one: one adult heart, studied with five tools: Watch the heart, Where should the sensor go?, How much noise can it take?, When electrodes fail, and Can I trust it?, which compares the twin with recordings from real people. Branch two: 42 scanned chests, studied in the virtual trial on the Evidence page and in the tool Sensor exploration.">
  <div class="tmap-row" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="tbox"><b>Chest scans</b><span>CT scans of real chests</span></div>
    <span class="tarrow"></span>
    <div class="tbox tbox-main"><b>Heart Twin</b><span>A simulated heart in a scanned chest</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="tmap-split" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="tbranch">
      <span class="tarrow"></span>
      <div class="tbox"><b>One adult heart</b><span>Five tools</span></div>
      <ol class="tlist">
        <li>Watch the heart</li>
        <li>Where should the sensor go?</li>
        <li>How much noise can it take?</li>
        <li>When electrodes fail</li>
        <li>Can I trust it? <em>Compares the twin with recordings from real people.</em></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="tbranch">
      <span class="tarrow"></span>
      <div class="tbox"><b>42 scanned chests</b><span>The same heart settings in every chest</span></div>
      <ul class="tlist">
        <li>The virtual trial <em>Its results are on the Evidence page.</em></li>
        <li>Sensor exploration <em>Tool 6: four design options, chest by chest.</em></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
